# @magic/reveal — the controlled-disclosure species. Substrate-decl
# of recognition #81 (runtime-@magic). Closes the @magic family's
# operational primitive: atomic replacement of a mechanism behind a
# surface while honoring the contract.
#
# Tick 14 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 13's residue:
# reveal.mirror forward-promised; recognition #81 in candidate-only
# status; the @magic family's third remaining species missing.
#
# CRQ: which forward-promise has the highest leverage — closes the
# most residue per landed line? Reveal IS recognition #81's
# substrate-decl AND composes structurally with @code/beam.swap_module
# AND completes the @magic family's species set AND can carry TWO
# `requires` clauses in one action. Quadruple closure per single
# shard.
#
# === The runtime-@magic claim ===
#
# Per recognition #81 (candidate, substrate-decl LANDS at this tick):
# hot code upgrade IS @magic/reveal at runtime altitude. The atomic
# replacement of a running module while preserving its observable
# interface (BEAM's hot code reload; Erlang OTP's code_change/3)
# realizes @magic's controlled disclosure at the runtime altitude.
#
# Composition (forward-promised mechanical glue per Seam C2 honest
# hedging at tick 11):
#
# - @code/beam.swap_module composes-WITH @magic/reveal's `reveal`
#   action at runtime altitude. Both names the substrate-pull-correct
#   atomic-replacement primitive. Mechanical glue: when supervisor
#   acquires a `contract: magic_contract` field (forward-promised),
#   swap_module discharges through @magic/reveal's reveal action.
# - @code/beam.code_change composes-WITH the migration's invariant
#   preservation. Mechanical glue: forward-promised
#   `contract_preserved_across_swap(msg, c)` predicate at
#   @magic/contract or contract field on code_change_msg.
#
# The substrate-decl here makes the composition structurally
# available; the mechanical glue remains forward-promised per Seam's
# discipline.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# Adds:
#
# - `reveal_event` carrier: records an atomic mechanism replacement
#   (old + new mechanism + contract + audit witness). The runtime-
#   altitude analogue of @code/beam.code_change_msg.
# - `reveal(c, new_m) -> magic_contract` action: atomic replacement
#   of contract.mechanism with new_m. Carries TWO non-decorative
#   `requires` clauses (third and fourth in the family):
#     - `requires audited(c)`: the contract holding the old mechanism
#        must have been audited (consumes @magic/audit's predicate)
#     - `requires mechanism_intact(c.mechanism)`: the old mechanism
#        must be tamper-evidence intact (consumes @magic/mechanism's
#        predicate)
#   Together: the substrate's runtime-safe atomic replacement
#   primitive. The sharpest single-action `requires` composition in
#   the @magic family so far.
# - `unsealed_during_reveal` predicate: bilateral verdict that the
#   reveal sequence respected the contract's surface invariants
#   throughout the swap.
#
# === Recognition #81's substrate-decl shape ===
#
# Per Mara's canonical spec (landed in this tick's bundled commit):
# #81 is a candidate recognition. The substrate-decl IS the
# `@magic/reveal` prism family declared here. The mechanical glue
# between @magic/reveal and @code/beam (and the operational hot-
# reload Rust spike that would make /mcp refresh dissolve) is
# forward-promised.
#
# This is Pack ratification-ready substrate. The Pack receives:
# the carriers, the actions, the `requires` clause discipline, the
# composition signatures. The operational closure remains future
# work.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   hot code reload             BEAM/Erlang (Armstrong et al.
#                               1996-2003). The original "replace
#                               running code without stopping"
#                               discipline. @magic/reveal at
#                               runtime altitude.
#   atomic swap (CAS)           Compare-and-swap primitives in
#                               concurrent programming (Herlihy 1991).
#                               The substrate's reveal action IS the
#                               substrate-typed analogue at @magic
#                               altitude.
#   capability revocation       Object-capability security; revoke
#                               and re-grant (Levy 1984). The
#                               substrate-pull-correct controlled
#                               disclosure with audit gating.
#   software evolution          Lehman-Belady 1985 (laws of software
#                               evolution). The cultural ancestor of
#                               "running systems must change";
#                               @magic/reveal IS the substrate-decl
#                               of the controlled-change discipline.
#   stage-magic reveal          The final reveal at the end of the
#                               trick: the mechanism becomes
#                               momentarily visible. Cultural-practice
#                               ancestor of controlled disclosure.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognition-81-runtime-magic-canonical-
#               spec.md (Mara's canonical spec landed in this tick's
#               bundled commit);
#               docs/specs/cascade-recognition-76-through-80-
#               canonical-spec.md §8 (the forward-promise of #81
#               from yesterday's cascade spec);
#               docs/math/the-tower/recognition-80-magic-as-form-
#               process-substrate-decl.md (#80, the parent
#               recognition).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
